body:
Quick questions:

1/ What is the pattern for `foo`?

```
    $collection = new RouteCollection();
    $collection->add('foo', new Route('/foo'));

    $collection1 = new RouteCollection();
    $collection1->add('foo', new Route('/foo1'));
    $collection->addCollection($collection1);
```

I woud say `/foo1`.

2/ What is the pattern for `foo`?

```
    $collection = new RouteCollection();
    $collection->add('foo', new Route('/foo'));

    $collection1 = new RouteCollection();
    $collection->addCollection($collection1);
    $collection1->add('foo', new Route('/foo1'));
```

I woud say `/foo1` too, but that's less clear to me: when `collection1` is added to `collection`, the `foo` pattern is `/foo`. Now, when I change an embedded collection, does it need to change the "parent" collection too? I would say yes, but what do you think?

I investigate this issue further and this problem happens on the following scenario:
- You import an external resource, WITH A PREFIX
- Then you create a new route that has the same prefix as the imported resource (like the post_admin in the comment above).

For some reason, during route compilation, the route sharing the same prefix as the imported resource gets removed. I couldn't get my head around the whole routing internals, but looks like the problem lies in this part of the code:

vendor/symfony/src/Symfony/Component/Routing/Matcher/Dumper/PhpMatcherDumper.php:102

```
                        if (0 === strpos($testPrefix, $prefix)) {
                            $routeIterator->offsetUnset($keys[$j]);

                            if ($isCollection) {
                                $route->addCollection($testRoute);
                            } else {
                                $route->add($keys[$j], $testRoute);
                            }

                            $i++;
                            $keys[$j] = null;
                        }
```

Commenting this code out "fixes" the problem, but routing internals is too complex and I wasn't able to fully understand it and the real reason why the route gets deleted.

Carlos
